 "pdf": "ads114s06.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3-4 (pins; pin 28 AVSS-SW), p.6 (ROC: DVDD 2.7-3.6 V, IOVDD DVDD-5.25 V), p.12-13 (timing: tp(CSDO) 25 ns, tp(SCDO) 30 ns, tp(CSDOZ) 25 ns), p.40 (Table 13 low-latency first-data times), p.43 (Table 15 sinc3), p.46-47 (global chop), p.51 (STATUS byte), p.54 (CRC-8-ATM), p.56-59 (reset, power-down, standby, conversion modes, programmable delay 14 tMOD default), p.60-61 (SPI mode 1, DOUT/DRDY, DRDY), p.62 (twos complement), p.63-66 (Table 24 commands, RREG/WREG), p.67-69 (read data direct, RDATA, full duplex), p.70-83 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog input, PGA, multiplexer, reference, IDACs, bias voltage, burn-out sources, system monitors, low-side switch PSW (stored only)",
  "GPIO0-3 on the analog pins (GPIODAT/GPIOCON stored only; the pins are analog in the model)",
  "PGA rail flags and reference monitor flags (STATUS bits 5-0 read 0); RDY flag during the 2.2 ms POR / td(RSSC) reset delay",
  "offset / gain calibration commands and the OFCAL/FSCAL correction of the result",
  "conversion time is the first-data time of Tables 13 / 15 (by FILTER and DR) plus the default 14 tMOD programmable delay; DELAY[2:0] settings other than 000, second and later continuous conversions (1 / data rate) and global chop (G_CHOP: Tables 18-19, about twice the time) are not modeled; internal 4.096 MHz oscillator (an external CLK scales the times; the CLK pin is not used)",
  "CRC byte: the pattern carries the CRC-8-ATM of the 0 V code (00h, or 0Bh after a STATUS byte of 80h); STATUS bits other than FL_POR are always 0 in the model, so these two values are exact for the model but the CRC is not computed",
  "read data direct: the data frame ([STATUS] result [CRC]) is shifted from every CS fall, not only after DRDY falls; with CS tied low no frame starts; data are not corrupted by serial activity after DRDY",
  "WREG to 02h-07h or 09h[7:5] restarts an ongoing conversion and clears the data (datasheet); not modeled",
  "START/SYNC low stops continuous conversions only after the ongoing conversion completes; the START command is not decoded while START/SYNC is high",
  "in power-down only RREG, RDATA and WAKEUP work; WREG and RESET wait for WAKEUP (all commands work in the model)",
  "commands are blocked during an RDATA / RREG reply and conversion data are not loaded during a register read (the model decodes bytes during replies); an RREG/RDATA during direct read corrupts the data",
  "after RDATA or direct read the data bytes repeat with continued SCLK (modeled idle repeat; the same repeat follows an RREG reply, where the datasheet gives zeros past the last register)",
  "DRDY returns high at the first SCLK edge after it falls (modeled: on result read); 24 tCLK high pulse when data are not read",
  "DOUT/DRDY: the datasheet drives it low with DRDY only while CS is low and holds it Hi-Z with CS high",
  "RREG/WREG beyond the last register (zeros / ignored); SPI timeout (TIMEOUT bit, 2^15 tCLK per byte); td(RSSC) 4096 tCLK reset delay"
 ],
 "variants": "ADS114S06 (6 inputs: pins 19-22, 31, 32 without AIN6-AIN11, DEV_ID 101b) and ADS114S08 (12 inputs, DEV_ID 100b) share ads114s06.pdf (SBAS815A, 2017). The B revisions ADS114S06B / ADS114S08B (ads114s06b.pdf, own spec files) drop the low-latency filter, conversion delay, global chop, rail / reference flags, STATUS byte / CRC output and direct read; their pin 28 is AVSS",
